**Add%20badge**%20button%20in%20the%20%3Ci%20class%3D%22fa%20fa-history%20fa-fw%22%3E%3C%2Fi%3E%20**Versions%20and%20GitHub%20Sync**%20panel.%20When%20pushed%20to%20GitHub%2C%20the%20badge%20shows%20your%20community%20where%20to%20participate%20the%20discussion%20or%20contribute%20to%20the%20documentation.%20%0A%0A!%5Bimage%5D(https%3A%2F%2Fhackmd.io%2F_uploads%2FHkcIFa3klg.png)%0A%0A%0A%23%23%23%20Push%20to%20GitHub%0AYou%20can%20choose%20which%20named%20versions%20to%20push%20to%20GitHub%20before%20the%20push.%20Each%20named%20version%20would%20be%20pushed%20as%20a%20%22commit%22%20in%20Git%2C%20while%20the%20version%20name%20and%20description%20will%20be%20used%20as%20its%20commit%20message.%0A%5BLearn%20How%20to%20Save%20a%20Version%5D(%2Fs%2Fhow-to-save).%0A%0A!%5BCHoose%20the%20version%20want%20to%20sync%20GitHub%5D(https%3A%2F%2Fhackmd.io%2F_uploads%2FrJiHo621el.gif)%0A%0A%0A%3A%3A%3Ainfo%0A%3Abulb%3A%20**Hint%3A**%20HackMD%20doesn't%20track%20which%20versions%20had%20been%20pushed%2C%20for%20this%20information%20would%20be%20misleading%20should%20someone%20else%20messes%20with%20the%20branch%20from%20GitHub%2C%20which%20HackMD%20could%20not%20know.%0A%3A%3A%3A%0A%0A%23%23%23%20Pull%20from%20GitHub%0AYou%20can%20also%20pull%20from%20GitHub%20and%20choose%20the%20branch%20you%20want%20to%20pull%20from.%20Moreover%2C%20you%20can%20choose%20which%20chunk%20of%20revisions%20to%20merge%20into%20your%20note%2C%20or%20apply%20all%20changes.%20%0A%0A!%5BPull%20from%20GitHub%5D(https%3A%2F%2Fhackmd.io%2F_uploads%2Fr1K1Rpnklg.gif)%0A%0A%0A%3A%3A%3Ainfo%0A%3Abulb%3A%20**Hint%3A**%20HackMD%20will%20automatically%20save%20a%20version%20before%20you%20merge%20and%20name%20it%20%60before%20pull%20from%20%3Cbranch_name%3E%60.%20Because%20HackMD%20doesn't%20lock%20the%20note%20when%20applying%20changes%2C%20it%20is%20possible%20that%20someone%20else%20edit%20your%20note%20while%20you're%20merging%2C%20therefore%2C%20%22undoing%22%20the%20merge%20has%20to%20be%20done%20in%20the%20editor.%20%0A%3A%3A%3A%0A---%0A%23%23%20Install%20the%20App%20on%20More%20Repos%0AIf%20you%20cannot%20find%20the%20repo%20you%20want%20to%20link%20to%2C%20cancel%20the%20synchronization%20first.%0A%0A!%5Bimage%5D(https%3A%2F%2Fhackmd.io%2F_uploads%2FB1gv9Tnklg.png)%0A%0AThen%2C%20you%20can%20re-authorize%20the%20app%20on%20more%20repos.%0A%0A!%5Bimage%5D(https%3A%2F%2Fhackmd.io%2F_uploads%2FrJOy5Thygg.png%20%3D350x)%0A%0A%3A%3A%3Ainfo%0A%3Abulb%3A%20**Hint%3A**%20Remember%20to%20refresh%20the%20repo%20list%20after%20you%20authorize%20new%20repos.%0A%3A%3A%3A%0A%0A%23%23%20Revoke%20Authorization%20and%20Un-installation%0AIf%20you%20ever%20want%20to%20revoke%20the%20account%20level%20authorization%2C%20this%20is%20where%20you%20would%20find%20the%20option%3A%20%5BClick%20here%5D(https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fsettings%2Fapps%2Fauthorizations)%0A%0AIf%20you%20ever%20want%20to%20un-install%20the%20app%20for%20your%20personal%20repos%2C%20find%20it%20here%3A%20%5BClick%20here%5D(https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fsettings%2Finstallations)%0A%0AFor%20un-installing%20your%20organization%20repos%2C%20find%20it%20here%2C%20you%20obviously%20need%20adequate%20permissions%3A%20%5BClick%20here%5D(https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Forganizations%2Fyour_organization_name%2Fsettings%2Finstallations)%0A%0A%3A%3A%3Awarning%0A%3Awarning%3A%20**Note%3A**%20Note%20that%20your%20account%20authorization%20and%20repo%20installation%20are%20separated.%20You%20could%20have%20revoked%20the%20account%20authorization%20(and%20the%20app%20could%20no%20longer%20see%20what%20repos%20you%20have%20access%20to)%2C%20yet%20keep%20the%20app%20installed%20on%20your%20repos%20(and%20you%20can%20still%20push%20to%20and%20pull%20from%20the%20repo).%0A%3A%3A%3A%0A%0A---%0A%23%23%20Line%20Break%20Rendering%20Rules%0AHackMD%20follows%20the%20%5BCommonMark%20Spec%5D(https%3A%2F%2Fspec.commonmark.org%2F0.29%2F)%20(the%20Spec)%20to%20render%20Markdown%20syntax%20so%20your%20notes%20would%20be%20compatible%20with%20other%20platforms.%20Yet%20there's%20one%20thing%20HackMD%20handles%20slightly%20differently%3A%20line%20breaks.%20%0A%0A%23%23%23%20What%20are%20line%20breaks%3F%0A%23%23%23%23%20Hard%20line%20breaks%0AWhen%20you%20hit%20the%20%3Ckbd%3EEnter%3C%2Fkbd%3E%20(or%20%3Ckbd%3EReturn%3C%2Fkbd%3E)%20key%20on%20your%20keyboard%2C%20you%20type%20a%20%22newline%22%20character.%20Since%20you%20most%20likely%20expect%20to%20start%20a%20new%20line%2C%20*HackMD*%20lets%20you%20continue%20on%20a%20new%20line%20(by%20rendering%20that%20%22newline%22%20character%20with%20a%20HTML%20break%20tag%20%60%3Cbr%20%2F%3E%60).%20This%20rendering%20behavior%20is%20called%20%5B**hard%20line%20break**%5D(https%3A%2F%2Fspec.commonmark.org%2F0.29%2F%23hard-line-breaks)%20in%20the%20Spec.%0A%0A!%5BHard%20line%20break%5D(https%3A%2F%2Fhackmd.io%2F_uploads%2FSk6wxR31xg.gif)%0A%0A%0A%23%23%23%23%20Soft%20line%20breaks%0AThere's%20another%20way%20to%20render%20the%20%22newline%22%20character%3A%20the%20%5B**soft%20line%20break**%5D(https%3A%2F%2Fspec.commonmark.org%2F0.29%2F%23soft-line-breaks)%20(or%20just%20line%20break).%20The%20newline%20character%20will%20be%20rendered%20as%20a%20%3Ckbd%3ESpace%3C%2Fkbd%3E%20in%20the%20HTML%2C%20instead%20of%20a%20new%20line.%20This%20is%20how%20**GitHub**%20and%20some%20other%20services%20handle%20line%20breaks.%0A%0A!%5BSoft%20line%20break%5D(https%3A%2F%2Fhackmd.io%2F_uploads%2FBk4we03kle.gif)%0A%0A%0AUnder%20this%20way%2C%20when%20you%20want%20to%20start%20on%20a%20new%20line%20(hard%20line%20break)%2C%20you%20could%3A%0A%0A**1.%20Type%20two%20or%20more%20spaces%20at%20the%20end%20of%20the%20line%2C%20before%20the%20newline%20character%3A**%0A%3E%20foo%20%3Ckbd%3ESpace%3C%2Fkbd%3E%20%3Ckbd%3ESpace%3C%2Fkbd%3E%20%3Ckbd%3EEnter%3C%2Fkbd%3E%0A%3E%20bar%0A%0A**2.%20Type%20a%20backslash%20at%20the%20end%20of%20the%20line%2C%20before%20the%20newline%20character%3A**%0A%3E%20foo%20%3Ckbd%3E%5C%20%3C%2Fkbd%3E%20%3Ckbd%3EEnter%3C%2Fkbd%3E%0A%3E%20bar%0A%0A%3A%3A%3Ainfo%0A%3Abulb%3A%20**Hint**%0A-%20Line%20breaks%20take%20effect%20only%20within%20the%20containing%20paragraph.%20If%20you%20want%20to%20start%20a%20new%20paragraph%2C%20just%20hit%20%3Ckbd%3EEnter%3C%2Fkbd%3E%20(or%20%3Ckbd%3EReturn%3C%2Fkbd%3E)%20twice.%0A-%20Technically%20HackMD%20is%20compliant%20with%20the%20Spec%2C%20according%20to%20the%20Spec%3A%20%0A%20%20%20%20%5B%E3%80%90A%20renderer%20may%20also%20provide%20an%20option%20to%20render%20soft%20line%20breaks%20as%20hard%20line%20breaks.%E3%80%91%5D(https%3A%2F%2Fspec.commonmark.org%2F0.29%2F%23soft-line-breaks)%0A%3A%3A%3A%0A%0A%23%23%23%20Should%20I%20care%3F%0ASince%20HackMD%20and%20GitHub%20renders%20line%20breaks%20differently%2C%20Your%20notes%20would%20look%20differently%20on%20the%20two%20platforms%20if%20the%20line%20break%20rendering%20rules%20are%20different.%20But%20if%20a%20note%20won't%20ever%20be%20pushed%20to%20GitHub%2C%20you%20don't%20have%20to%20worry%20about%20this.%20%0A%0A%23%23%23%20How%20do%20I%20change%20my%20line%20break%20rendering%20rule%3F%0A%0A1.%20You%20can%20change%20your%20default%20line%20break%20rendering%20for%20all%20your%20future%20notes%20in%20your%20%5B%3Ci%20class%3D%22fa%20fa-gear%20fa-fw%22%3E%3C%2Fi%3E%20**settings**%5D(https%3A%2F%2Fhackmd.io%2Fsettings%23note).%0A2.%20You%20can%20click%20the%20%3Ckbd%3EBreaks%3C%2Fkbd%3E%20button%20at%20the%20bottom%20of%20the%20editor%20to%20choose%20your%20line%20break%20rendering%20rule.%0A%0A!%5BChange%20Line%20break%20rules%5D(https%3A%2F%2Fhackmd.io%2F_uploads%2FHyijiT3kel.gif)%0A%0A","viewMode":"publish","unreadState":["comment"],"isOwner":false,"isSignIn":false,"isLiked":false,"isBookmarked":false,"publishType":"view","commentCount":14,"isNotesRecommendationsEnabled":true,"lastChangeUserInfo":{"name":"Andy","path":"Andy-hackmd","avatarUrl":"https%3A%2F%2Fwww.gravatar.com%2Favatar%2F1ef8a4e3e62dda92a633b9ce81cf53aa%3Fs%3D96"}}`);
